# i18n

Locales: `en-US` (default, guilhermeguain.com) and `pt-BR` (guilhermeguain.com.br). Detection is off; switching uses `router.push(asPath, asPath, { locale })`.

- One JSON file per namespace under `public/locales/{locale}/`.
- Namespaces: `common`, `meta`, `menu`, `hero`, `about`, `hard-skills`, `soft-skills`, `data-driven-seo`, `experience`, `projects`, `education`, `events`.
- Always add/change keys in **both** `en-US` and `pt-BR`. Keep key trees identical.
- Nested objects are fine (`experience.ifood.role`). Components read them as `t('experience:ifood.role')`.
- New namespace: create both JSON files **and** add the name to `serverSideTranslations` in `src/pages/index.tsx`.
- Do not put user-facing copy in hooks or JSX when it belongs in locale JSON. Tech badge titles (`React.js`) may stay in code.
